Package: patrone-hyperv-setup
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, apt, pkexec, systemd
Description: Virtual Machine Setup: gets Patrone Linux ready for Hyper-V
 At each desktop login in a Hyper-V virtual machine, Virtual Machine Setup
 checks what Patrone Linux needs there, and if something's missing, shows
 a dialog that offers to set it up with one administrator's password:
 Hyper-V's integration services (patrone-guest-tools) and VMConnect's
 enhanced session (patrone-remote-desktop's service for it). For what has
 to change on Windows, the VM's enhanced session transport and any
 integration service turned off for it, it shows the PowerShell command to
 run there, with a Copy button. "Don't show this again" turns it off for
 the account.
 .
 It runs only in Hyper-V virtual machines (systemd's
 ConditionVirtualization), never in the installer's live session, and shows
 nothing when everything is set up.
 .
 Hyper-V and Windows are trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies.
